'''Volisanian Baliscans''' ({{Lang-ca|Baliscans volisenys}}; {{Lang-bl|Baliscanos volisanyanos}}) refers to [[Baliscans]] citizens of full or partial [[Volisanian people|Volisanian]] ancestry or persons born in the [[Kingdom of Volisania]] who reside in [[Balisca]]. Volisanian Baliscans form the largest [[Illypnian Baliscans|Illypnian ancestry]] group in the confederation. Between 1857 and 1946, 261,020 Volisanian people immigrated to Balisca, predominately to [[Cerdanya]] and [[Estuaria]]. Besides immigration from the [[Volisan Countries|Volisan Communities]], Balisca also received, as early as the 1840s, immigrants with Volisanian background from other former [[Volisanian sphere|Volisanian colonies]], notably [[Volistraya]], which bolstered the community.

Baliscans of Volisanian descent make up a substantial proportion of the Baliscan population, and have historically played an integral role in the socioeconomic development of the [[Baliscan archipelago]] (i.e. [[Volisan aristocracy]]).

